      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-325721",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/c6/c6211ffc8fcf297e7181fdc364d5f2c4f3c032f3e33d4b507de907d152fa1219.png)\n\nA neighborhood book club surveyed $36$ members. For each member, the average time spent reading on a typical day ($x$, in hours) and the average time spent discussing books ($y$, in hours) were recorded to the nearest half hour. The scatter plot above shows the data with a line of best fit.\n\nThe line of best fit **overestimates** one member\u2019s reported discussion time by more than $1.5$ hours. How many hours did this member report reading?"
